fear:
Like shot from guns. On, on. And now she had cast
The voices off with the uplands. On. Mad fear
Was running in her feet and killing the ground;

feasts:
Leisure or labor or work day or play day--
Feasts for the famous and fun for the fool;
Phyllis, ah, Phyllis, my life is a gray day.

feasting:
I passed the door, and saw my friends
Feasting beneath green orange boughs;
From hand to hand they pushed the wine,

fearfully:
And showering down the stars like sudden rain.
And evermore men shall go fearfully
Bending beneath their weight of heaviness;

fearlessly:
And he was no soft-tongued apologist;
He spoke straightforward, fearlessly uncowed;
The sunlight of his truth dispelled the mist,

feast:
And here is Life: the vines in the vale
And friend and foe, and the feast in the hall,
And May and the maid, and the glen and the grail;

feat:
And, like a clock, winds with withoutness willed
What should have been an inner instinct’s feat;
Or as a prose-wit, harshly poet turned,

fearless:
Which must, I know, yet be the corner-stone
Of all believing,--birds now flying fearless
Across would drop in terror to the earth;

Brave shines the sun through the freckled pane;
Fearless the cobweb swings from the ceiling --
Indolent housewife, in daisies lain!

fearsome:
With a prime deceit to pin it;
And I thought I was gaining a fearsome prize,
So I staked my soul to win it.

featherweed:
The seed burrs all with laughter crack
On featherweed and jimson;
And leaves that should be dressed in black

feahed:
Dough I 's all a-trimble
Feahed some one 'll see;
Bet in a half a minute

feather'd:
Divine Apollo sends a second dart;
Swift thro' his throat the feather'd mischief flies,
Bereft of sense, he drops his head, and dies.

With clouds incompass'd glorious Phoebus stands;
The feather'd vengeance quiv'ring in his hands.
Near Cadmus' walls a plain extended lay,

On ev'ry leaf the gentle zephyr plays;
Harmonious lays the feather'd race resume,
Dart the bright eye, and shake the painted plume.

feast's:
His feet that cannot carry him.
My feast's a show, my lights are dim;
Be still, your music is not sweet,--

feastful:
This only can I tell: that hour by hour
I waxed more feastful, lifted up and glad;
I felt no thorn-prick when I plucked a flower,

fealty:
Contracting parties should be equal, just;
But if, a simple fealty on one side,
A mere religion,—right to give, is all,

fear's:
Suddenly turns round, nothing to detect,
Yet on his fear’s sense keepeth still the load
Of that brink-nothing he doth but suspect;
